package "pkg/builtins/reflect"

// TypeOf / DataOf are compiler intrinsics (spec §7.13.14): a DIRECT call
// `reflect.TypeOf(x)` / `reflect.DataOf(x)` is lowered inline (OP_IFACE_TYPEINFO /
// OP_EXTRACT, gen_call.bn) with no call to the bodies below.  These bodies exist
// for the NON-inlined path — the function taken as a value, or dispatched by name
// through the bytecode VM's package-function registry — so the
// `pkg/builtins/reflect.{TypeOf,DataOf}` symbol resolves instead of dangling.
// They must match the intrinsic lowering exactly.
//
// An interface value (`*any`) is two words passed BY VALUE — the data pointer at
// index 0 (IfaceValueDataIndex) and the vtable pointer at index 1
// (IfaceValueVtableIndex); the dynamic `*TypeInfo` is the vtable's slot 1.  `&x`
// is a pointer to that 2-word value; reading its words yields the fields.  The
// param is a raw (unmanaged) `TYP_INTERFACE_VALUE`, so it is borrowed — no entry
// RefInc, no scope-exit RefDec — and these bodies only read through it.  They do
// NOT call TypeOf / DataOf, so no bare `reflect.*` call spelling is produced from
// within the package (which gen_call.bn's fully-qualified-only intrinsic match
// relies on).
//
// TypeOf depends on word 1 being a NATIVE `@__ivt` vtable POINTER — true because
// reflect is injected interface-only (interp/externs.bn), so this body is only
// ever the NATIVE compiled symbol (a VM func-value call routes to it), never
// interpreted.  A VM-built interface value instead carries a 1-based
// vm.IfaceVtables INDEX in word 1 (lower_call.bn), so interpreting this body would
// deref an index-as-pointer; do NOT load reflect's `.bn` fully into the VM.
// (DataOf is representation-independent — word 0 is the data pointer either way.)

// TypeOf returns the dynamic `*TypeInfo` for the value boxed in x — the vtable
// (interface word 1) slot-1 pointer.
func TypeOf(x *any) *TypeInfo {
	var w **uint8 = bit_cast(**uint8, &x) // &x: pointer to the 2-word value
	var vt **uint8 = bit_cast(**uint8, w[1]) // interface word 1 = vtable pointer
	return bit_cast(*TypeInfo, vt[1]) // vtable slot 1 = *TypeInfo
}

// DataOf returns the raw address of the value boxed in x — the interface value's
// data word (word 0).
func DataOf(x *any) *uint8 {
	var w **uint8 = bit_cast(**uint8, &x)
	return w[0] // interface word 0 = data pointer
}
